{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-1401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $u$ has magnitude $6$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $7,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${134}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to one decimal place where appropriate." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-1401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =6\\cdot 7\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{134}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =42\\cdot (0.719\\,33…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(30.212\\,27…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈30.2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-1401" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd689e7606ce64e3a8a4114e430dcdc6803d2459fc131d007b0f3f0c431e63c5"} {"question" "q-1401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-1401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "19.6n"] ["math" "23.0n"] ["math" "26.5n"] ["math" "27.8n"] ["math" "30.2n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-1401" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30.2n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $u$ has magnitude $1$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $11,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${27}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ Round your final answer to the nearest integer where appropriate." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =1\\cdot 11\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{27}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =11\\cdot (0.453\\,99…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(4.993\\,89…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd689e7606ce64e3a8a4114e430dcdc6803d2459fc131d007b0f3f0c431e63c5"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11n"] ["math" "3n"] ["math" "5n"] ["math" "6n"] ["math" "7n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-127844" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5n"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-146304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $u$ has magnitude $2,$ the vector $v$ has magnitude $5,$ and the angle between the vectors is ${0}^{∘}.$ What is $u\\times v?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-146304" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $u$ and $v$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $u\\times v=0$ if and only if $u∥v.$\n\nSince the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${0}^{∘},$ our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $u\\times v=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d