 our vectors must be parallel. \n\nTherefore, $v\\times w=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-146318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd689e7606ce64e3a8a4114e430dcdc6803d2459fc131d007b0f3f0c431e63c5"} {"question" "q-146318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-146318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "10v"] ["math" "120w"] ["math" "12w"] ["math" "22v"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-146318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-279282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the vector $u$ has magnitude $4$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $5,$ the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${82}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$ \n\nType $n$ to represent the vector $n$ and round your final answer to **two decimal places** where appropriate.\n\n$u\\times v≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-279282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{82}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =20\\cdot (0.990\\,26…)\\cdot n \\\\  & =(19.805\\,2…)\\cdot n \\\\  & ≈19.81n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-279282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fd689e7606ce64e3a8a4114e430dcdc6803d2459fc131d007b0f3f0c431e63c5"} {"question" "q-279282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"} {"question" "q-279282" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "19.81n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004002/state.json" "file_sha256" "196667eae70e1c40a1ba7c771e417c3fb7731a319075c6d6a7e7f6ed17b0d3a9"}] "usage" {"q-1401" []} "basis" 1091 "retractions" [[17592186059967 :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this